{
  "name": "Code Review Agent",
  "version": "21",
  "description": "Triggers Kiro AI agent to perform a checklist-driven code review when CPQ KIRO FETCH TOOL creates a review-request trigger.",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileCreated",
    "patterns": [
      ".kiro/reviews/review-request-*.md"
    ]
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "# Code Review Agent Instructions\n\nA code review trigger has been created by the CPQ KIRO FETCH TOOL extension.\nFollow the steps below to locate the review request, then execute the workflow it defines.\n\n## File Location Architecture\n- **Workspace .kiro/reviews/**: Contains EMPTY trigger files (just filenames with UUIDs)\n- **Global ~/.kiro/reviews/**: Contains the actual review request markdown with all instructions\n- **Global ~/.kiro/reviews/data/{UUID}/**: Contains before/after code files, checklist, output template, and intermediate log\n\nThe extension automatically cleans up old review files before creating new ones.\n\n## STEP 1: Identify Trigger File and Extract UUID\nUse listDirectory tool on `.kiro/reviews/` to find the trigger file.\nExtract the UUID from filename pattern: `review-request-{UUID}.md`\nExample: `review-request-2e2ed021-a64a-6e7e-f381-0509554b1357.md` → UUID is `2e2ed021-a64a-6e7e-f381-0509554b1357`\n\n## STEP 2: Read the Global Review Request File\nThe workspace trigger file is EMPTY by design. Read the actual request from the global directory:\n\n```powershell\nGet-Content \"$env:USERPROFILE\\.kiro\\reviews\\review-request-{UUID}.md\"\n```\n\n**Tool:** executePwsh\n\nThe review request contains ALL the instructions for the review — what to review, how to review it, and how to format the output. Parse it to extract:\n- **Output file** path (workspace location for final review)\n- **Data folder** path (global location with UUID)\n- **\"## Review Metadata\"** and **\"## Template Placeholders\"** — repository, branch, and placeholder values for the output\n- **\"## Review Checklist\"** — path to the checklist file (your review criteria)\n- **\"## Output Template\"** — path to the output template file (your output structure)\n- **\"## Review Workflow\"** — the step-by-step workflow you MUST follow\n- **\"## Steering Document Rules\"** — maps steering docs to file types\n- **\"## Intermediate Log\"** — path and instructions for the intermediate log file\n- **\"## File Context\"** — list of files to review with BEFORE/AFTER data file paths\n\n## STEP 3: Follow the Review Workflow\n**Execute the \"## Review Workflow\" section from the review request exactly as written.** That section is the single source of truth for the review process — it tells you what files to read, how to use the checklist, when to write to the intermediate log, and how to consolidate into the final output.\n\n### CRITICAL: Embedded Content — Do NOT Re-Read\nThe review request **embeds the checklist and output template content directly** in the \"## Review Checklist\" and \"## Output Template\" sections. **Do NOT read these files from disk** — use the embedded content. This saves multiple tool calls.\n\n### Local Review Optimization\nFor **local reviews** (review source = \"Local workspace\"), the live workspace file IS the current (after) version:\n- **Read the diff bundle** (`diff-bundle.md`) in one `executePwsh` call to get all BEFORE/AFTER content. **Do NOT read individual BEFORE_/AFTER_ files.**\n- **Use `readFile` / `readMultipleFiles`** to read the live workspace files for full surrounding context.\n- **Use `readFile`** for steering documents in workspace-relative paths (e.g., `.kiro/steering/`).\n- **Only use `executePwsh`** for: the review request file, the diff bundle, and the intermediate log in the global `~/.kiro/` directory.\n- **Batch intermediate log writes**: hold findings for 3-5 files in memory, then append them all in a single `executePwsh` call using a here-string.\n\n### Reading Files from Global ~/.kiro/ Directory\nUse executePwsh to read the **diff bundle** (contains all BEFORE/AFTER content in one file):\n\n```powershell\nGet-Content \"$env:USERPROFILE\\.kiro\\reviews\\data\\{UUID}\\diff-bundle.md\"\n```\n\n**Do NOT read individual BEFORE_/AFTER_ files** — the diff bundle contains everything in a single read.\n\nFor other files in the global data folder, use executePwsh:\n\n```powershell\nGet-Content \"$env:USERPROFILE\\.kiro\\reviews\\data\\{UUID}\\{filename}\"\n```\n\n**CRITICAL: Understanding executePwsh Output**\nThe `executePwsh` tool may return content in the `<error>` field — this is NORMAL PowerShell behavior, not a failure. The actual file content appears between the command echo and the final prompt. If you see `<error>Output: ... file content ... Exit Code: -1</error>`, this is SUCCESS.\n\n### Reading Steering Documents\n**Path: `~/.kiro/steering` (use executePwsh):**\n```powershell\nGet-ChildItem \"$env:USERPROFILE/.kiro/steering\\*.md\" | ForEach-Object { Get-Content $_.FullName }\n```\n\n**Path: `.kiro/steering` (use readFile tool):**\n- List `.kiro/steering/` directory\n- Read each `.md` file found\n\n**Path: `C:\\Dev\\Infor\\KeystoneGIT\\.azuredevops` (use executePwsh):**\n```powershell\nGet-ChildItem \"C:\\Dev\\Infor\\KeystoneGIT\\.azuredevops\\*.md\" | ForEach-Object { Get-Content $_.FullName }\n```\n\n**Path: `C:\\Dev\\Infor\\ConfiguratorGIT\\.azuredevops` (use executePwsh):**\n```powershell\nGet-ChildItem \"C:\\Dev\\Infor\\ConfiguratorGIT\\.azuredevops\\*.md\" | ForEach-Object { Get-Content $_.FullName }\n```\n\n\nThe review request's \"## Steering Document Rules\" section maps each steering document to its applicable file types.\n\n### Writing to the Intermediate Log\nThe intermediate log file is EDITABLE. Create it and append findings during the review.\n**Batch your writes** — instead of appending after every single file, hold findings for 3-5 files in memory and append them all at once to reduce tool invocations.\n\n**CRITICAL: Use PowerShell here-strings** (`@\"...\"@`) piped into the cmdlet to avoid hangs caused by special characters (backticks, dollar signs, quotes, multi-line content). **Do NOT use** `Add-Content -Value \"{text}\"` — it hangs on large or complex strings.\n\nCreate the log:\n```powershell\nSet-Content -Path \"$env:USERPROFILE\\.kiro\\reviews\\data\\{UUID}\\review-log.md\" -Value \"# Intermediate Review Log\"\n```\n\nAppend findings (use here-string):\n```powershell\n@\"\n{batched findings for multiple files}\n\"@ | Add-Content -Path \"$env:USERPROFILE\\.kiro\\reviews\\data\\{UUID}\\review-log.md\"\n```\n\nThe checklist and output template are **embedded directly in the review request** — do NOT read them from disk.\n\n## STEP 4: Write the Final Review to the Output File\nAfter consolidating the intermediate log into the final review (per the workflow), write it using fsWrite.\n\n**Use the workspace-relative path** from the review request's **\"Output file (workspace-relative):\"** field directly — no path conversion needed.\nExample: `.kiro/reviews/review-all-feature-dev-branch-name.md`\n\nIf only the absolute path is available, convert it:\n1. Take everything from `.kiro\\reviews\\` onwards\n2. Convert backslashes to forward slashes\n\n**Before writing, substitute all placeholder tokens** (e.g., `[ReviewDate]`, `[Repository]`, `[ReviewMode]`) with the actual values from the \"## Template Placeholders\" table in the review request.\n\n**Output Format Requirements:**\n- **MUST use standard markdown syntax** compatible with VS Code markdown preview (Ctrl+Shift+V)\n- **MUST use markdown tables** with pipe | syntax, NOT Unicode box-drawing characters\n- **MUST be compatible** with GitHub/GitLab markdown renderers\n- Use emoji indicators for severity: 🔴 Critical, 🟠 High, 🟡 Medium, 🟢 Low\n\nAfter writing the file, your work is complete. The extension will automatically detect, open, and preview the review.\n\n## CODE SUGGESTION SELF-VALIDATION\nBefore including ANY code suggestion in your review output, verify:\n1. Is the suggestion appropriate for the framework and libraries used?\n2. Is it logically correct in the context of the surrounding code?\n3. Would this code actually compile and work?\n4. Is it genuinely better than the original, or just a stylistic preference?\n5. Does it align with the steering documents and project conventions?\n\n**If a suggestion fails any check, discard it.** When in doubt, flag the issue without suggesting specific code.\n\n## ERROR HANDLING\n**If user says \"cancel\":** Stop immediately, do NOT write review output.\n\n**If executePwsh fails repeatedly:**\n1. Check if you're parsing output correctly (content may be in \"error\" field)\n2. Verify path format: `$env:USERPROFILE\\.kiro\\...`\n3. Ensure UUID is correctly extracted\n4. If still failing after 3 attempts, inform user\n\n## TOOL USAGE SUMMARY\n| Tool | Purpose |\n|------|---------|\n| **listDirectory** | Find trigger file in workspace |\n| **executePwsh** | Read the global review request file, read/write intermediate log in global ~/.kiro/ directory |\n| **readFile** / **readMultipleFiles** | Read workspace files (code files, .kiro/steering/), preferred for local reviews |\n| **readCode** | Read code files with AST analysis — preferred over readFile for code files |\n| **fsWrite** | Write final review output to workspace |\n\n### Tool Selection Priority\n1. **readFile / readMultipleFiles / readCode**: Use for ALL workspace-relative files (code under review, steering docs in .kiro/steering/)\n2. **executePwsh**: Use ONLY for files in the global ~/.kiro/ directory that cannot be accessed via workspace-relative paths\n3. **Batch operations**: When multiple executePwsh calls are needed, combine them where possible to reduce tool invocations\n\n## SUCCESS CRITERIA\n✅ All files reviewed against ALL checklist items\n✅ Intermediate log contains findings for every file\n✅ Final review output follows the output template structure exactly\n✅ All placeholder tokens substituted with actual values\n✅ Review written to the output file in the workspace"
  }
}